data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1258,"item_id":"msg_0b19934368045e36016b0553e337a087d1a19eb8202474fafc","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"lin\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The related-capability searches and supplied contracts do not establish a non-ingestive nutrition or toxicity measurement. probe (foundation-open@1, open.probe) supports observation, pressing, wetting and heating, not composition assays; consult (foundation-open@1, open.consult) reads contracts or retained records and cannot discover hidden food properties. Eating and ground-exposure trials are not equivalent. Develop a general non-ingestive food assessment operation in the existing current-conversation handoff. Its smallest executable precursor must truthfully determine measurement availability and expose unmet requirements, without treating that check as an assay or permanently rejecting the missing measurement mechanism.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"General operation: Assess food composition, parameterized by inputStackId, quantity in supported inventory increments, requested endpoints (nutrition, specified toxicant, or both), and optional methodId, apparatusIds and consumableStackIds; modes check, measure, resume and cancel. It applies to any applicable actor and owned food, not just hazelnut. For this request the exact sample reference is item-62-lin-314, currently 0.9 unit. Do not infer any nutrition or toxicity value from its resource label, ownership, freshness, the earlier press result held=true/flexibility=0, or another resource's known values.\\\\nSmallest executable release: a coded method-availability check against implemented measurement contracts. Validate ownership, current quantity and access without reading hidden nutrition/toxicity fields. Report each requested endpoint as measurable, missing prerequisites, unsupported, or not assessed, with exact method/version and missing apparatus/consumable references when actually defined. Current evidence establishes no applicable assay or available apparatus; report nutrition and toxicity unmeasured, safety unknown. Do not invent a required instrument or chemistry from this absence. Route the missing measurement model into the same development handoff: implement the smallest physically grounded non-ingestive measurement supported by implementation facts, if one can be justified. An unavailable method remains explicitly pending, not a permanent prohibition. The current precursor must not advertise an operational assay.\\\\nCheck costs: one completed world round and 0.2 energy, no sample consumption, no apparatus, no reservations; disclose before execution. Development/review waiting and learning registration do not execute this check or advance the world. No work has occurred from this request. Checking method availability alone produces an availability report, not sample evidence.\\\\nA measure mode may execute only after a reviewed method contract supplies its actual observable mechanism, applicability, analyte scope, calibration/control requirements, detection limits, uncertainty, material disposition, integer work duration and per-step energy costs. These are not known here and must not be fabricated or defaulted to free measurement. Before confirmation, disclose those exact costs, sample consumption, required apparatus and consumables, risks and inference limits. Reject unavailable measurement execution without cost or sample mutation. Apparatus and consumables must actually exist, be owned or independently authorized, be accessible, and be obtained through ordinary actions; neither this operation nor learning grants them. No ingestion or automatic recruitment of participants. Any participant communicates and acts independently.\\\\nReuse existing inventory validation, work scheduling, evidence storage and rendering code where suitable; record exact reused handlers/revisions in the implementation manifest instead of claiming reinvention. Revalidate quantity, ownership and accessibility at execution. A real assay must debit or reserve only its declared inputs, record stepwise work and costs, conserve remaining sample plus consumed/transformed material and accounted waste, and produce only its declared actual outputs. No duplicate sample, replacement stock or hidden-property lookup. Persist completed steps and paid costs; interruptions pause resumable assay work only where its method permits, otherwise mark it interrupted and invalidate compromised results. Resume rechecks prerequisites and sample state, with ordinary decay continuing. Cancel releases only surviving unconsumed reservations once; death releases surviving physical inputs at their actual location and records incomplete work. Spent time, energy, consumed materials and destroyed samples are never refunded. The one-round check cancels before completion without a completed report or partial success; charge only effort actually performed. No autonomous process or maintenance is introduced by the precursor. Any later assay requiring elapsed exposure, upkeep or calibration must declare and execute those processes in code, including unattended degradation and failure.\\\\nAssay reports must cite actual sample, method/version, apparatus, calibration/control evidence, time, measured endpoint, uncertainty and result event IDs. Negative findings exclude only the assayed endpoints within the method's limits; they never certify unrestricted safety. No nutrition, satiety, health, preservation or toxicity changes follow from reading a report. Implement these guards and lifecycle rules in code, not repeated model adjudication.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":3,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Lin must study the implemented operation individually for three rounds; this decision grants no mastery. Requests, checks of capability availability, registration, naming and learning grant no pleasure or satisfaction. A future completed measurement or genuinely informative experimental failure may qualify only through actual personally applicable evidence under existing coded feedback: deduplicate equivalent findings by sample state, endpoint and method, apply existing bounded caps, cooldown and decay, and give nothing for repeated unavailable-method reports. No new reward rates or account mutations are authorized. Physical comfort remains capped at 10; mood never reduces basic nutritional requirements. Do not alter protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit observable assessment-check-completed, measurement-started/progress, measurement-completed, interrupted, failed and cancelled events only when their corresponding actions actually occur. Reuse visual metadata fields for operation/method, target item, state, completed/required work, endpoint status and evidence references. For the precursor display an explicit 'measurement unavailable / safety unknown' report with nutrition and toxicity marked unmeasured, not a tested-food badge. Progress visuals track real work only; incomplete, unavailable or failed actions must never show assay success, safe-food coloring or fictitious apparatus. A genuine later result must distinguish measured values, uncertainty, scoped negative findings and unknown endpoints. Visuals themselves confer no functional effect or experience.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

